         <p>Let \(A = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1.2 \\ 1.2 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\). Its eigenvalues are \(1 \pm 1.2\), namely \(2.2\) and \(-0.2\). Eigenvectors are \((1, 1)^{\top}\) for \(2.2\) and \((1, -1)^{\top}\) for \(-0.2\), since \(A (1, 1)^{\top} = (2.2, 2.2)^{\top}\) and \(A (1, -1)^{\top} = (-0.2, 0.2)^{\top}\). With the orthogonal matrix \(Q\) whose columns are \((1, 1)^{\top}/\sqrt{2}\) and \((1, -1)^{\top}/\sqrt{2}\), the spectral decomposition is \(A = Q\,\diag(2.2, -0.2)\,Q^{\top}\).</p>
